      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Qwen Image 2.1: img2img, references\n\nThe Qwen Image 2.1 workflow for img2img. Write full sentences in the\norder subject → action → setting → lighting/camera → style, and put literal text in quotes.\n\n**Settings**: 25 steps, CFG 1, euler, simple, 1248×832 drafts (multiples of 32). At CFG 1 the negative prompt is\nunused; raise CFG only together with a negative prompt (it doubles the compute).\n\n## img2img\n\nThe image of **Load Image ib:img** is the starting point: **Resize to** scales it to the size of the Generate tab\n(Width / Height, its *Resize to* in img2img mode; **Use size** in the Input cell takes the size of the image),\n**VAE Encode** makes the latent, and the sampler adds noise by the **denoising** strength (0.6 here) and samples\nfrom there. The prompt describes the whole image you want. Low denoising keeps the composition and colors; high\ndenoising moves further from the image. To change one area only, use the inpaint workflow; to change the image by\nan instruction, an edit model with references.\n\nThe Generate tab is in **img2img** mode while this workflow is loaded. Send an image with **Send to the input\nimage** (B), from the editor, or upload it in the Input cell before the first queue. This workflow has no Hires.\nfix pass: upscale the result with the full workflow.\n\n## Image Bench\n\n| Marker | Node | Generate tab |\n|--------|------|--------------|\n| `ib:cp` | Load Diffusion Model | model list, model exploration |\n| `ib:img` | Load Image | Input cell; Send to the input image (B), the editor |\n| `ib:pp` | Image Bench Prompt | prompt and LoRA list |\n| `ib:np` | Text Encode Qwen Image 2.1 | negative prompt (its `negative_prompt` widget) |\n| `ib:smp` | KSampler | seed, steps, CFG scale, sampling method, schedule type; denoising; Resize to (the Resize to node) |\n| `ib:ref:0-3` | Reference 1-4 (bypassed) | References panel |\n| `ib:lora` | Load LoRA (bypassed) | LoRA exploration only |\n\n**References** (up to 4; the encoder takes up to 16, connect more loaders marked `ib:ref:4`, ...): add images\nin the References panel of the Generate tab, by \"Ps sends to: reference\" from Photoshop, or by dropping them\nthere. They go into the `images` inputs of **Text Encode Qwen Image 2.1**, which shows them to the Qwen3-VL encoder\nand splices their VAE latents into the sequence (resized to about `resolution`² pixels). An empty slot is bypassed,\nwhich leaves its encoder input unconnected. For edits, generate at the size of the first reference: any other\nsize shifts the edit.\n\nPut any ESRGAN-type model into\n`models/upscale_models` ([RealESRGAN_x4plus.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Real-ESRGAN_repackaged/resolve/main/RealESRGAN_x4plus.safetensors) here).\n\n**LoRAs**: check them in the LoRA list or type `<lora:name:weight>` into the prompt.\n\nThe ControlNet tab has no units here: no ControlNet exists for Qwen Image 2.1 (the Qwen-Image ControlNets are for\nthe 20B model); give a pose or depth map as a reference instead.\n\n## Model Links\n\n**diffusion_models**: [qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/resolve/main/diffusion_models/qwen_image_2.1_int8_convrot.safetensors)\n**text_encoders**: [qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_8b_int8_convrot.safetensors)\n**vae**: [qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1/resolve/main/vae/qwen_image_2.1_vae_bf16.safetensors)\n\nQwen Image 2.1 is released under the Qwen Research License (non-commercial).\n"
      ],
      "title": "Note: Qwen Image 2.1 (Image Bench, img2img)",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
